@consumer = http://localhost:4134/odata/v4/shop

### Response cache — run this twice.
### 1st call: cache miss → upstream request (see provider terminal).
### 2nd identical call within 30s: cache hit → NO upstream request.
GET {{consumer}}/CachedCustomers

### Same query signature → served from response cache
GET {{consumer}}/CachedCustomers

### A DIFFERENT query signature is a separate cache entry (response strategy)
GET {{consumer}}/CachedCustomers?$filter=country eq 'DE'

### Entity cache — first call warms a full SQLite snapshot...
GET {{consumer}}/EntityCachedCustomers

### ...then ANY filter/orderby is answered from SQLite until TTL (no upstream call)
GET {{consumer}}/EntityCachedCustomers?$filter=country eq 'DE'&$orderby=name desc

### Product response cache with a custom tag ('product-cache')
GET {{consumer}}/CachedProducts
